  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nActive weather looks to hold for the long term period as present\ntrends in models see the Panhandles open up to new disturbances\nfollowing the exit of the trough to our north. These disturbances\nwill look to take advantage of the monsoonal moisture that is\nexpected to keep pushing in from our southwest and bring us daily\nchance of showers and thunderstorms through next week. For Monday,\nthese chances do look to start mostly in the Southern Texas\nPanhandles with expectations to spread further north as new trough\nmoves into the Southwestern Untied States Tuesday. After which,\nmodel agreement does try to break down the trough with its\nremnants pushing east and aiding us in another round of activity\nWednesday. Beyond this point, model agreement begins to break down\nwith GFS keeping more short-wave activity over the area clear into\nnext weekend while the ECMWF actually tries to force the remnants\nof a tropical system up into New Mexico, which could result in\nmuch stronger activity for the end of the week. Regardless all\nthis active weather is expected to keep the Panhandles cool for\nall of next week with highs in the mid 70s to 80s starting Monday.",
